 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And May is all sweet the shadow\nOf a crowd of wistful snow\nThat keepeth home, to let out again\nTheir things that they have taken.\nO gentle April leafy breezes free\nFrom the red and black old leaves on every\nTree's face, O sighing sky-heron away\nHis boundless song for thee! - say not, saying\nI shall wait thine hour, away\nFor the moon to light again\nThe shining gates and starry hallways. See\nThe stars at last be ready",
